cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use WarmMemory in research, please cite it using these metadata."
title: "WarmMemory: a capacity-bounded warm-memory layer for LLM agents with LangGraph integration"
version: 0.3.0
date-released: 2026-05-18
type: software
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/vsingh45/WarmMemory"
url: "https://github.com/vsingh45/WarmMemory"
abstract: >-
  WarmMemory is a Python package for short-term memory management in LLM
  agents. It provides a capacity-bounded warm-memory buffer, a pluggable
  importance scoring interface, a LangGraph BaseStore implementation with
  per-namespace eviction, and a benchmark that compares full-history,
  vector-only, and warm-fallback retrieval strategies.
authors:
  - family-names: Singh
    given-names: Vivek
keywords:
  - llm-agents
  - short-term-memory
  - langgraph
  - retrieval
  - benchmark
